  "reply_to_user": "Hi Hannah, thanks for getting in touch. You're right: Duo was never set up on your account, and the VPN won't let you in until it is. That's common with newly issued laptops and easy to fix. Setup takes about 10–15 minutes with one of our technicians, either remotely or in person, and you'll need your phone with you. During the session we'll install the Duo Mobile app on your phone, have you scan a setup code, and send a test notification to make sure everything works. Could you reply with: (1) a few times you're free over the next day or two (your hours are 9 AM–5 PM Eastern, right?), (2) whether you'd like to do it remotely or in person, and (3) whether your phone is an iPhone or Android. Until then you may not be able to use the VPN. If you're in the office, you can keep working on the office network without it. Also, your account is set to ask you for a new password at your next sign-in, so you'll see that prompt too. That's expected.",
  "internal_note": "User: Hannah Lee (user_id 12), Finance Payroll Specialist, not a VIP. Account is active, sign-in isn't blocked, VPN access is on, 0 failed logins, must_change_password=true (password set 2026-10-09 14:26 UTC). Duo check: enrolled=false, no device. Laptop BL-LT-0112 (Win 11) is online, last check-in 2026-10-09 14:14 UTC, no warnings. Sign-in logs: 9 successful sign-ins from New York, all around 09:04 local, corporate and residential IPs only, no hosting networks, no failed passwords or mfa_denied. No KB-031 red flags. Earlier VPN sign-ins (most recent 10/07) worked with mfa=none, so Duo enforcement seems to have only just started applying to this account (new laptop or policy change). Worth confirming that's expected. No action tools were queued because none apply. Next step per KB-004: book a remote or in-person enrollment session with the user present and her phone in hand, install Duo Mobile, install the Duo client on BL-LT-0112 if it's missing, have her scan the activation QR code, and send a test push. Waiting on the user for availability and phone type. Until enrollment is done she may not be able to use VPN.",
